=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
The VLAN 5 bridge interface `br_v5` on sshswitch has been administratively brought
down (it carries no UP or LOWER_UP flags, reports state DOWN). `br_v5` is the Layer-3
SVI for Campus 2 VLAN 5 and hosts the default gateway address 10.5.0.254/24. With
this bridge down, all inter-subnet traffic from PC1, PC2, and dc_pc5 is dropped at
the first hop: ARP for 10.5.0.254 goes unanswered, and PC1 reports "Destination Host
Unreachable" when pinging the gateway directly.

Intra-VLAN pings (PC1 ↔ PC2) continue to work because switch4 bridges those frames
locally within br_vlan5 without needing the gateway, which is why users can still
reach each other.

The NOC's hypothesis — a failed trunk uplink on sshswitch — is incorrect. The
physical trunk (sshswitch eth0, on segment ms1_sw4) is UP and LOWER_UP, the VLAN 5
sub-interface (eth0.5) is also UP, and the peer VLAN 6 bridge (br_v6) is fully
operational. Only `br_v5` is down. This is a software-level administrative shutdown
of the bridge, not a physical cable or port failure.

Root cause: `br_v5` on sshswitch was administratively disabled, taking down the VLAN
5 default gateway (10.5.0.254) while leaving the physical trunk intact.

Corrective fix: On sshswitch run `ip link set br_v5 up`. This immediately restores the
gateway and inter-subnet routing for all VLAN 5 hosts. To make it persistent, ensure
the bridge is brought up in the device's startup configuration.
=== END ===
